I must disagree;  all arquebus( sp plurual) are muskets, not all
muskets are arqubuses.

It's a bit like saying " a 1946 Ford, also known as an automobile".
The Arqubus is a particular kind of early musket preceding the
flintlock, noted for being unreliable and having a slow load time. The
"Brown Bess" flintlock of the 18th century could fire 3 rounds in a
minute ... so that's once every two or three game turns, yes?
Whereas the arquebus could only fire a round every 20 minutes ...
that's about 60 turns of re-loading. Seems more balanced to me that
way, preserving the late-medieval "feel" of Nethack.

